NOTICE — php2shell-detect

This project independently develops:
  - php2shell.py (detection scanner, tier architecture, verdict logic)
  - the lab configuration, differential harness, and measured matrices

It builds on publicly disclosed research for CVE-2026-109618 /
CVE-2026-109619:

  * The stale-PS(id) arm/read leak field layouts used by the T2 oracle were
    first demonstrated by:
      unlimit0118/CVE-2026-109619-php2shell-poc
      https://github.com/unlimit0118/CVE-2026-109619-php2shell-poc
    (functional parameters — field counts, sizes, offsets — re-implemented
    here; no upstream code is redistributed in this repository)

  * The P1-P5 primitive documentation, official patch-diff analysis, ASAN
    convictions, and the 18-shot negative matrix referenced in our
    limitations are from:
      WoYinDao/CVE-2026-109618-CVSS-9.2-Critical
      https://github.com/WoYinDao/CVE-2026-109618-CVSS-9.2-Critical

  * The scanner-precedent and the patched-build false-positive behavior we
    correct were observed in:
      pentestershell/php2shellbt
      https://github.com/pentestershell/php2shellbt

